        "answer": {
          "short": "In the given $x$ order,\n$$x^2:\\quad 4,\\ 1,\\ 0,\\ 1,\\ 4,\\ 9.$$\n$$(x-1)^2:\\quad 9,\\ 4,\\ 1,\\ 0,\\ 1,\\ 4.$$",
          "worked": "Substitute each given value of $x$ into both expressions. For example, at $x=-2$,\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2&=(-2)^2=4\\\\(x-1)^2&=(-2-1)^2=9.\\end{align*}$$\nThe completed rows, in the given $x$ order, are\n$$x^2:\\quad 4,\\ 1,\\ 0,\\ 1,\\ 4,\\ 9,$$\n$$(x-1)^2:\\quad 9,\\ 4,\\ 1,\\ 0,\\ 1,\\ 4.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0
      },
